findings.finding:
Several new rules are still untested, and the README's mutation claim covers only the builder's own list. I ran 30 further single-point mutants through the published runner's full logic: cases, texts, selection rows, header, and both embeddings with MAS-RA-003's check_log. 13 non-equivalent mutants pass every vector, and the model answers each case correctly in my probes. The surviving rules:
- held-out by task ID in the same suite: N02 ignores task ids, N03 accepts any suite (only the content-digest route is tested, by T49);
- 'a stored record must hash to its key' for topologies (transcript N10, binding N09) and manifests (N08), and _stored without its hash check (N07); probe P09 shows a misfiled topology correctly answered UNKNOWN_REFERENCE;
- scope subjectType BOARD_CLAIM (N14; probe P03);
- the transcript part of subjectId (N15, see M4R2-1);
- a third ledger in a claim's history (N18, which uses only the last previous ledger; probe P05: PASS, then FAIL, then a PASS re-judging the first PASS's evidence is correctly VERDICT_HISTORY via HISTORY_RETRY);
- VERDICT_NOT_PASS before WORK_MISMATCH (N20; probe P06);
- MODE for a central transcript whose id is a node id (N22; probe P07);
- leases expiring after the deadline (N23): the round-1 behaviour passes every vector. The model is fixed (probe P04: a lease ending at 3560, next operation at 3601, gives i1 OPEN with an EXPIRY at 3560), but B01's expiries all happen at operations before the deadline, so the M4R1-4 disposition ('B01's board and gaps record them') does not pin the fix;
- the kinds pin (the builder's M46): killed only by the extra wrong-kinds check in tools/masra004/mutants.py, not by the published vectors or runner;
- the binding's schemaVersion (N13).
The builder's equivalence claims hold:
- M06, M07 and M08 are each equivalent alone. An OPEN item's verdicts are unobservable (VERIFY there is NOT_HELD, MERGE NOT_HOLDER), and every way back to HELD resets them. The three together are killed.
- M15 is equivalent. ASSIGN needs a COORDINATOR agent, MODE_STRUCTURE allows none on the board, and SINGLE_AGENT has no board.
My own equivalents: N19 (one subject per claim, so the first and the latest verdicts name the same work), N24, N25 (the scope shape equals scope_digest's rule), and N26/N27 (redundant with _stored).

findings.requiredChange:
Add vectors until each non-equivalent survivor above is killed:
- a record whose DEVELOPMENT task id is held out in the same suite (another suite must not count);
- a topology and a manifest stored under a key they do not hash to;
- a bound scope with another subjectType;
- a cross-transcript ledger;
- a valid three-ledger history and a HISTORY_RETRY one;
- a MERGE with a FAIL latest verdict and the wrong work;
- a central transcript id equal to a node id;
- a lease that ends before the deadline, processed only by a post-deadline operation;
- a runner check that a wrong kinds record is UNKNOWN_REFERENCE;
- a binding with a wrong schemaVersion.
Reword the README's mutation sentence to name the list it covers.
